    "landmark_semantics": "Anatomical left/right. Landmarks x,y normalized by source width/height. Use source-pixel coordinates for distances and angles (multiply x by width, y by height). Point10 is forehead/face oval, NOT top of hair/head. Iris centers are not calibrated gaze targets.",
    "matrix": {
      "property": "result.facialTransformationMatrixes[0]",
      "shape": [
        4,
        4
      ],
      "js_data_layout": "column-major",
      "at_row_col": "data[column*4+row]",
      "translation_indices": [
        12,
        13,
        14
      ],
      "last_row_indices": [
        3,
        7,
        11,
        15
      ],
      "last_row_expected": [
        0,
        0,
        0,
        1
      ],
      "mapping": "canonical face to observed/runtime metric face; includes uniform scale, rotation, translation",
      "space": "Right-handed virtual-camera metric space; x right, y up, virtual camera points down negative z. Normalized screen landmarks instead have y downward. Matrix is not camera extrinsic calibration or physical head distance.",
      "evidence": "geometry_pipeline.cc -> MatrixDataProtoFromMatrix; matrix.cc copies Eigen storage and clears layout; MatrixData default COLUMN_MAJOR; JS addFacialTransformationMatrixes copies packed data unchanged.",
      "formal_euler_convention": "If explicitly defining R=Rz(roll)*Ry(yaw)*Rx(pitch) with column vectors and positive uniform scale: pitch=atan2(data[6],data[10]); yaw=atan2(-data[2],hypot(data[0],data[1])); roll=atan2(data[1],data[0]). Radians. This is a chosen mathematical decomposition, not a vendor-certified biometric pose metric. Degenerate/nonfinite matrices must yield unknown; avoid gimbal-lock region.",
      "pose_guidance": "Use relative orientation magnitude as a UX hint after device testing; generic pitch prompt is safer than inferring whether the phone or head moved. Up/down reposition prompts can use source-frame face position. Validate sign with unmirrored inputs. Avoid claiming legal angular compliance or publishing uncalibrated exact degrees."
    },
    "operational_notes": [
      "VIDEO can reuse tracking. Temporal smoothing is applied for numFaces=1. numFaces is a maximum, so numFaces=1 cannot prove exactly one person is present; retain a separate multi-face detector check.",
      "The task calls are synchronous; throttle to available CPU throughput and avoid duplicate decoded frames. No paid API or image upload is needed.",
      "Use source dimensions/object-fit crop and mirror transform consistently for overlay mapping. Close the task on disposal; stop camera stream separately.",
      "For live UX, use temporal persistence/hysteresis and an unknown state for missing/unstable outputs. Thresholds and smoothing durations are product heuristics needing QA.",
      "Do not interpret coefficients or mesh as proof of identity, liveness, directed gaze, eye visibility compliance, official biometric quality or acceptance probability. Head pose is relative to a virtual camera; cannot separate head and phone motion."
    ]
